  FRAMING (conservative):
   Homology leakage predicts recall RISING with identity. Across the well-populated bins
   (50-69%, 70-100%; n>=20) recall shows NO positive association with identity (if anything the reverse) -- so the recovery is not
   near-twin memorization. No significance is attached to the magnitude of the decrease.
   Boundary tested: KR domains share a conserved fold -- the lowest occupied bin is 40%+ (no silent KR below it), consistent with the ~35% identity floor; very-distant transfer is
   not in the corpus to test, so this BOUNDS leakage rather than probing arbitrary distance.
